# Apps whose Allow in the Menu Bar value is pinned
# (System Settings → Menu Bar → Allow in the Menu Bar).
# macconfig-check.sh reads trackedApplications in the Control Center group
# plist via lib/menubar-allow.py. An app in this list that is allowed when
# it should be off is drift (Needs Paul). The check never writes the plist,
# and there is no --fix: the blob is undocumented and Control Center may
# overwrite it.
#
# An app that is not installed, or not in trackedApplications yet, is an
# info line, not drift. Anything not listed here is left as it is
# (Tailscale, Hammerspoon, Fleet Desktop, Karabiner, Okta, SentinelAgent, …).
#
# Format: bundle-id | on|off | display name
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored. Keep the display
# names in the menubar-third-party-hide title in lib/manual-steps.list.

com.1password.1password|off|1Password
com.todesktop.230313mzl4w4u92|off|Cursor
co.anysphere.cursor.nightly|off|Cursor Nightly
com.docker.docker|off|Docker
com.granola.app|off|Granola
com.microsoft.teams2|off|Microsoft Teams
com.tinyspeck.slackmacgap|off|Slack
us.zoom.xos|off|Zoom
com.raycast.macos|off|Raycast
com.logi.cp-dev-mgr|off|Logi Options+
notion.id|off|Notion
